{"name":"Derbyshire","hex":"#245e36","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Derbyshire","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A midland county of England bounded by South Yorkshire, West Yorkshire, Greater Manchester, Leicestershire, Nottinghamshire, Staffordshire and Cheshire.","A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Derbyshire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Derbyshire","blocks":[{"text":"Derbyshire is a ceremonial county in the East Midlands of England. It borders Greater Manchester to the north-west, West Yorkshire to the north, South Yorkshire to the north and north-east, Nottinghamshire to the east, Leicestershire to the south-east, Staffordshire to the south and west, and Cheshire to the west. The city of Derby is the largest settlement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Near_Hathersage%2C_Peak_District_8_%28cropped%2C_edited%29.jpg/330px-Near_Hathersage%2C_Peak_District_8_%28cropped%2C_edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derbyshire","wikidata":"Q23098"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Iron_Gate%2C_Derby_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4912062_%28cropped%2C_edited%29.jpg/500px-Iron_Gate%2C_Derby_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4912062_%28cropped%2C_edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Iron_Gate%2C_Derby_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4912062_%28cropped%2C_edited%29.jpg/500px-Iron_Gate%2C_Derby_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4912062_%28cropped%2C_edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIron_Gate%2C_Derby_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4912062_(cropped%2C_edited).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Masson_Mill_in_Matlock_Bath_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2631130.jpg/500